{
  "notes": "Outrun at night, F# minor, 116 BPM, pumping hard. A saw pluck (ANALOG TRAP PLUCK) runs eighth-note arpeggios up through each chord, a resonant phase-distortion bass (PHASE CZ BASS) gallops in sixteenths (one eighth, two sixteenths), the player's sync lead on the Smart Keys (TRIO SYNC LEAD, with an eighth-note echo), and the 909 kit on four on the floor with offbeat open hats; every kick ducks the synths. Scenes: A idles on i and VI in soft power-chord stabs; B drives i VI III VII; C is a two-bar lift, VI VII into i, with the arpeggio climbing an octave higher; D coasts on iv and VI in a wide room. ENERGY: the arpeggio alone in quarter notes, then kick, bass and eighths, then snare, clap and hats, then sixteenth hats, every note, ratchets and fills. All material is original.",
